 Prefer three strong reviewers over many vague reviewers.
 
+For a broad or multi-file review, do one cheap parent-level repository index
+pass before launch (for example the relevant instructions, `git status`,
+`git diff --stat`, and the likely file list). Include that same compact factual
+index in each reviewer task so workers do not all spend their first turns
+rediscovering the scope. Do not share conclusions or claimed bugs in the index,
+and require every reviewer to open and verify the relevant source independently.
+Skip this index pass when the target is already narrow and explicit.
+
 Give every reviewer a specific task prompt naming its angle. Ask reviewers to return concise, evidence-backed findings with file/line references and suggested fixes. The response should be review feedback, not a context summary. Reviewers must not edit files unless I explicitly ask for a writer pass.
 
 While reviewers run, do your own narrow inspection if useful. After they return, synthesize the feedback into:
